# Copy to apps/server/.env and adjust for your machine.
# This file documents every variable the server reads.
#
# For a real deployment, see README.md "Production deployment" and
# CONTEXT.md "Production deployment architecture" — none of the values
# below (secrets included) are meant to be reused in production; generate
# fresh ones.

# --- Server ---
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=4000
# Comma-separated list of allowed browser origins (desktop's Vite dev
# server, Expo web, a packaged app's origin, ...). Requests with no
# Origin header at all (native mobile fetch, curl) are always allowed, as
# is the literal "null" origin a packaged Electron app sends when loaded
# via file:// — only needed here for an actual browser-origin client. Add
# :8081 if you're running the mobile app with `expo start --web` for
# local testing.
#
# PRODUCTION: set this to your real desktop/web origins ONLY — never "*".
# A native mobile build needs nothing added here (no Origin header).
CLIENT_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:8081

# --- Database (PostgreSQL via Prisma) ---
# PRODUCTION: your hosting platform provides this (Railway/Render/Fly.io
# inject it automatically when you attach their managed Postgres, or you
# set it by hand for a self-managed Postgres/RDS/Supabase instance). Never
# commit a real value.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://msph:msph_dev_password@localhost:5432/msph_dev?schema=public"

# --- Auth ---
# Generate strong random secrets for real environments, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# PRODUCTION: MUST be different, real random values — never reuse these
# dev placeholders, and never commit the real ones.
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=dev-access-secret-change-me
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=dev-refresh-secret-change-me
JWT_ACCESS_TTL=15m
JWT_REFRESH_TTL=30d

# --- File storage ---
# "local" (default): LocalStorageDriver (src/storage/) writes real
# uploaded files under STORAGE_LOCAL_ROOT and serves them from
# STORAGE_PUBLIC_URL. Fine for local dev; NOT fine for production — a
# container's local disk is ephemeral on every platform in the deployment
# doc (gone on every redeploy/restart), and doesn't survive more than one
# replica either way.
#
# "s3": any S3-compatible object store — real AWS S3, Cloudflare R2,
# Backblaze B2, Supabase Storage's S3-compatible endpoint, or a
# self-hosted MinIO all work through the same driver (src/storage/
# s3StorageDriver.ts). This is what PRODUCTION should use.
STORAGE_DRIVER=local
STORAGE_LOCAL_ROOT=./storage/uploads
STORAGE_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:4000/uploads

# Only read when STORAGE_DRIVER=s3 — the server refuses to start with a
# clear error naming exactly what's missing if you set STORAGE_DRIVER=s3
# without these. Example values for Cloudflare R2 (a good low-cost
# default — no egress fees):
#
#   STORAGE_BUCKET=msph-photos
#   STORAGE_REGION=auto
#   STORAGE_ENDPOINT=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
#   STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY=<r2 access key id>
#   STORAGE_SECRET_KEY=<r2 secret access key>
#   STORAGE_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
#   STORAGE_PUBLIC_URL_BASE=https://photos.your-production-domain.example
#
# For real AWS S3 instead: omit STORAGE_ENDPOINT and
# STORAGE_FORCE_PATH_STYLE (both default correctly for AWS), set
# STORAGE_REGION to the bucket's real region (e.g. eu-west-1).
#
# STORAGE_PUBLIC_URL_BASE is optional even with STORAGE_DRIVER=s3 — a
# CDN/custom domain fronting the bucket. Omit it to serve directly from
# the bucket/endpoint's own URL (requires the bucket to allow public
# read on the uploaded objects).
STORAGE_BUCKET=
STORAGE_REGION=
STORAGE_ENDPOINT=
STORAGE_ACCESS_KEY=
STORAGE_SECRET_KEY=
STORAGE_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=false
STORAGE_PUBLIC_URL_BASE=

# --- Reverse proxy / TLS termination ---
# Not an env var — trust proxy is derived automatically from NODE_ENV
# (see src/app.ts): production trusts exactly one proxy hop (the norm for
# Railway/Render/Fly.io/a single Nginx in front of this process), so
# req.ip (what the login rate limiter keys on) reflects the real client,
# not the proxy. A deployment with an *extra* hop in front (e.g.
# Cloudflare -> Nginx -> this process) needs that value raised in
# src/app.ts — see its comment.
